# Copy to agents/guard.conf in this repo. The plugin's hooks read THIS repo's agents/guard.conf
# (via AGENTS_REPO), never a copy inside the plugin. The file is parsed, never executed: KEY='value'
# lines only, no variables or substitutions. Patterns are extended regular expressions joined with "|".
#
# Two lists. DENY = refused in every session, whatever the mode (H1, H2, H4_NEVER_PATHS below, and the
# permission deny rules in settings). ASK = "owner's hand": in a session you are sitting in, the agent gets a
# permission prompt and your answer is the go for exactly that command; an unattended run (AGENT_ROLE set)
# is refused and has to stage the action for you. The ask shapes the hooks know without config: host
# reboot/power-off, storage-layout tools, recursive rm on system paths, helm uninstall, kubectl delete of
# anything but a pod or job, force pushes, git history rewrites, deleting/resetting the main branch.

# H1 (deny) - any command matching these is blocked in every session (case-insensitive; also checked on MCP
# tool calls and WebFetch). Put here the people or shared
# channels that must NEVER receive an automated message: a person's device name, a broadcast
# target, a shared group channel. Never put a secret here.
# Examples: a partner's or child's phone name (pat-phone), a family group chat name, a team or club
# channel, a mailing-list address. Suggested default: everyone you live with plus any group chat you
# are in; adding an entry is free and you can remove it later.
# Pick identifiers that appear only in a send (a device name, a channel id). A bare first name
# also blocks reading commands and file paths that merely mention the person - by design, but you
# will feel it. An empty value turns H1 off.
H1_PATTERNS='<never-message-this-person>|<other-shared-channel>'

# H4_NEVER_PATHS (deny) - folders whose contents an agent may never delete, in any mode, not even with your
# tap. A command that names one is blocked when it is: `rm -r` (flags before or after the path, -r/-R/-rf/
# --recursive), `xargs rm -r` fed from a command that names the folder, `find ... -delete`, `find ... -exec rm`
# or `-ok rm`, `rsync --delete*` or `--remove-source-files`, `unlink`, or `shred`. (A `rsync --delete` that
# only READS from such a folder is blocked too; the guard cannot tell source from destination.) Photos,
# documents, finance, anything you keep the only copy of. Examples: the photo library, scanned documents,
# tax and finance records, family videos, a "keep" folder. Suggested default: every folder that holds the
# only copy of something; also list them in roadmap/home-setup.md ("Things I would hate to lose"). Empty =
# off. LIMIT: it matches paths NAMED in the command (`rm -rf /path/to/photos/x`,
# `find /path/to/photos -delete`). It does NOT see `cd /path/to/photos && rm -rf *`, a glob that expands
# to the folder, or a deletion made from inside a script or interpreter. Keep real backups of these folders.
H4_NEVER_PATHS='/path/to/photos|/path/to/documents|_keep'

# H4_PROVIDER_HOSTS (ask) - hosts whose API changes state you cannot undo (DNS provider, registrar). A
# write call (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE, --data) to one asks you when you are at the keyboard and is refused
# in an unattended run. Reads pass. Examples: your domain registrar's or DNS provider's API host, a
# cloud storage or backup service's API host, your router maker's cloud console. Suggested default:
# none, if you own no domain or such account (leave the placeholder; it matches nothing real).
H4_PROVIDER_HOSTS='api.dns-provider.example'

# H4_ASK_PATTERNS (ask) - your own "my hand" commands, as one regular expression: a deploy script, a
# production cluster, a particular namespace. Same behaviour as above. Examples: `deploy.sh`,
# `ssh nas`, `kubectl[^;&|]* -n production`, `terraform apply`. Suggested default: empty (only the
# built-in shapes); the value below is a placeholder, replace or clear it.
H4_ASK_PATTERNS='deploy-to-prod|kubectl[^;&|]* -n production'
